 >>[2026-07-22 17:08] observe — index-config.ts's IndexConfig/resolveIndexConfig has zero consumers (grep across spw-cli, spw-lsp) — a documented schema with no wiring yet. Leaving as-is; wiring it into query.ts or the LSP server-index is a real feature commit, not a rounding-off edit.
 >>[2026-07-22 17:10] observe — prompts/image.prompt.spw and prompts/song.prompt.spw had unquoted bareword values containing →/—/; that the lexer chokes on outside string context (parser.test.ts's 'parses prompt fixtures without lexer errors' requires zero tokenize errors, stricter than the general spw-syntax-validate.ts audit which only requires overall parse success). Fixed: quoted the two bareword values carrying an em-dash/semicolon, replaced → with -> in a # comment. prompts/website.prompt.spw was already clean. One pre-existing unrelated failure remains (isProseCommentLine('// note') expected true, returns false) — not part of this working tree's diff, left alone.
 >>[2026-07-22 17:15] taste — frontend/backend Spw runtime interaction (exploratory, not implemented): packages/spw-runtime (substrate.ts, pipeline/, interpreter/) is the execution backend; packages/spw-lsp (stdio-server.ts) + extensions/vscode-spw are today's only frontend. Today's LSP surface is diagnostics/hover/codeAction-shaped (static analysis), not live execution feedback. range-transform.ts's plan->apply-under-effect.l* shape (just fixed) is exactly the kind of round-trip a richer frontend would need: editor requests a plan (effect.l0.measure), shows a preview, host confirms, LSP calls applyRangePlan (effect.l2.workspace) and pushes the result back. Worth a future plan once there's a concrete frontend surface (web UI vs. VS Code webview) driving the question, rather than speculative runtime scaffolding now — see spw-feature-planning's own caution against building AST/protocol shape ahead of a real consumer.
 >>[2026-07-22 17:30] implement — agentic-development utility pass: (1) SPW_MATH_IDIOMS (math/idioms.ts) was defined but invisible from any CLI command despite being a complementary, more agent-useful catalog than FORMULA_CATALOG -- it pairs surface syntax with a falsify claim (e.g. 'select.armCount != frame content length', 'foldReady true with argCount < 2') that's checkable against real ONF fields normalize.ts now computes. Added `spw formula --idioms` (+ --family filter, +json). (2) index-config.ts's IndexConfig/resolveIndexConfig had zero consumers anywhere -- wired it into corpus-scan.ts's scanCorpus() (maxFiles caps the file list; annotations/operatorCensus gate the corresponding per-file heuristic calls) and exposed a shared `--depth minimal|standard|full` flag (via a new exported parseIndexDepth helper in corpus-scan.ts, avoiding 4x duplicated parsing) across all four sense-loop commands: formula, invent, map, analyze.
 >>[2026-07-22 17:32] verify — tsc --noEmit clean repo-wide; test:cli 90/90; manually confirmed --depth minimal actually suppresses annotations/sigils output in `spw invent` (ann=0, sigils=—) vs default/full showing real values.
 >>[2026-07-22 17:33] open — user raised a much broader ask mid-session ('enhance tooling value for script ecology, knowledgebase development, kinds of media, reasons for prompts, prep for dense learning material and expert-level density across domains') -- logged as ?[tooling-value-broad-scope] rather than folded into this bounded wiring pass; needs its own scoping conversation.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[epistemic-grade-name]: "What should E0/E1/E2 be renamed to? Candidate mirroring effect.l*: epistemic.e0.fact / epistemic.e1.score / epistemic.e2.report — needs confirmation before any doc edits in that family."
 ?[membrane-body-shape]: "Should membrane become a modifier field on BodyNode (e.g. BodyNode.membrane?: MembraneSpec) or a distinct wrapping AST node? Blocks track B entirely."
 ?[operator-products-scope]: "'New operator products' — is this asking for new composition algebra in types/coupling.ts, or new concrete operator sigils? Needs a concrete example from the user."
 ?[temporal-subtree-depth]: "'Runtime architectural preparedness for temporal/subtree linguistics' — is this a docs-only readiness note in docs/runtime/, or actual scaffolding (new interfaces/types) in packages/spw-runtime with no behavior yet?"
 ?[track-b-sequencing]: "Confirm track B (named params, multi-arm select, stream fold, new operator products, membrane+body) is deferred to follow-up plans rather than attempted in this branch."
 ?[plan-history-exclusion]: "Confirm: historical .agents/plans/*/{wip.spw,PLAN.md,*.spw} keep their original S0-S3/E0-E2 text as-written (retained operational memory), and only living docs/theory + docs/design + docs/audits + .spw/conventions + prompts + SKILL.md get renamed."
 ?[prose-naming-collision]: "'Prose' currently means two different things: # lines (real isProseCommentLine treatment, tolerant reflow) vs. unquoted bareword values inside braces (raw token stream, breaks on arbitrary punctuation — root cause of the image.prompt.spw/song.prompt.spw lexer errors just fixed by quoting). Give bareword-value positions real prose semantics too, or keep the split and stop calling unquoted brace values 'prose' so future authors don't assume they're lexer-safe the way # comments are?"
 ?[tooling-value-broad-scope]: "User asked to 'enhance tooling value for script ecology, knowledgebase development, kinds of media, reasons for prompts, prep for dense learning material and expert-level density across domains' -- too broad/abstract to scope alone; needs a follow-up conversation to pick a concrete first slice (which domain, which command, what 'expert-level density' means operationally)."
}

